Subject: the file list gives a VMS text file's size as LF lines

A VMS text record file (variable-length or VFC records with carriage
control) is sent as its LF lines (D3), whose size is not its size on
disk. flist_copy_stat() is where every file list entry takes its size.

--- a/flist.c	2026-11-06 19:47:33.183901476 +0000
+++ b/flist.c	2026-11-06 19:47:33.247110870 +0000
@@ -288,7 +288,15 @@
 	f->st.mode = st->st_mode;
 	f->st.uid = st->st_uid;
 	f->st.gid = st->st_gid;
+#ifdef __VMS
+	/*
+	 * A VMS text record file goes as its LF lines, which is not the
+	 * size on disk (vms/vms_at.c).
+	 */
+	f->st.size = f->path != NULL ? vms_lf_size(f->path, st) : st->st_size;
+#else
 	f->st.size = st->st_size;
+#endif
 	f->st.mtime = st->st_mtime;
 	f->st.rdev = st->st_rdev;
 	f->st.device = st->st_dev;
